TY  - JOUR
DB  - Ovid MEDLINE(R) <1988 to 1995>
ID  - 7635034
T1  - Acarbose for non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus.
DO  - https://dx.doi.org/10.1136/dtb.1994.32751
A1  - Anonymous
Y1  - 1994//
N2  - Acarbose (Glucobay-Bayer) is the first in a new class of oral antidiabetic drugs, the alpha-glucosidase inhibitors. It is licensed for the treatment of patients with non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus (NIDDM), either as first-line therapy when dietary measures are insufficient, or as an adjunct to conventional oral therapy where glycaemic control is suboptimal. The manufacturer claims that acarbose "can achieve a new level of blood glucose control in diabetes". In this article we consider whether acarbose offers any real advance.
