T1  - Reduced plasma membrane Ca2+-ATPase function in platelets from patients with non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus.
A1  - Rosado, Juan Antonio
A1  - Saavedra, Francisco Raul
A1  - Redondo, Pedro Cosme
A1  - Hernandez-Cruz, Juan Manuel
A1  - Salido, Gines Maria
A1  - Pariente, Jose Antonio
Y1  - 2004//
N2  - We clearly show that plasma membrane Ca2+ ATPase (PMCA) activity is lower in platelets from patients with non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus (NIDDM) than in those from healthy controls. The lower activity is likely due to reduced PMCA expression and increased tyrosine phosphorylation. These findings provide an explanation for the cellular ionic defects occurring in insulin resistant conditions.
