T2  - Vliianie akarbozy (gliukobaia) na lipidnyi metabolizm bol'nykh insulinonezavisimym sakharnym diabetom.
A1  - Rosliakova, L V
A1  - Roitman, A P
A1  - Ametov, A S
A1  - Dolgov, V V
Y1  - 2000//
N2  - AIM: To investigate the effect of acarbose, intestinal alpha-glucosidase inhibitor, on lipid metabolism in patients with non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus (NIDDM)., MATERIAL AND METHODS: Glucobai was given for 6 months in a dose 300 mg/day to 63 NIDDM patients aged 40-69 years. The examination covered indices of glycemia, glycosylated hemoglobin, pancreatic insulin secretion, total cholesterol (TC), triglycerides (TG), HDLP and LDLP cholesterol, atherogenic index., RESULTS: Glucobai has improved glycemic profile, reduced insulinemia and body mass index, TC, TG, atherogenic index. Blood levels of HDLP cholesterol elevated by 62%., CONCLUSION: Long-term intake of acarbose improves carbohydrate metabolism and produces a hypolipidemic effect.
