N2  - Combination therapy, using drugs from different classes of oral hypoglycemic agents, offers several advantages in the treatment of non-insulin-dependent diabetes mellitus (NIDDM). Appropriate combinations can significantly improve glycemia and often obviate insulin treatment. In general, no increased toxicity or significant interactions are observed.
